CREATED:20260427T211634Z
DESCRIPTION:Title of Presentation:\n"Trusting Your Knots - A Journey throu
 gh Surgery and Climbing"\n\nSpeaker:\nImran Anwar\, MD\nChief Resident\, 
 General Surgery\n\nTitle of Presentation:\n"Interdisciplinary De-escalati
 on in Breast Cancer Care"\n\nSpeaker:\nAmanda Nash\, MD\nChief Resident\,
  General Surgery\n\nChief Talks consists of exit presentations given by C
 hief Residents from the General Surgery and Cardiothoracic residency prog
 rams. Each Resident will give a 15-20 minute presentation followed by a 1
 0 minute Q&A session.  This talk will be recorded and made available for 
 on-demand viewing. Please visit our website linked below for access.\n\nT
 he mission of Surgery Grand Rounds is to provide an educational format th
 at has a broad appeal to Duke faculty\, residents\, staff\, and students.
  Grand Rounds consists of a broad range of topics that are presented by l
 ocal\, regional\, and international speakers on clinical education\, rese
 arch science\, and developments in technology\, and also addresses other 
 related issues that may affect our current and future surgeons. Physician
 s who attend Surgery Grand Rounds are eligible to receive CME credit.\n\n
 For more information\, please visit our website by clicking on MORE EVENT
  INFORMATION below
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260427T211634Z
